[TITLE]
NUM-36: groundwater recession, no rain, no evaporation, 4 days.
10-acre aquifer, water table 8 ft above the bottom, drains to J1 (invert 2 ft)
with A1 = 0.05, B1 = 1.5. The only flux out of the aquifer is the lateral
groundwater flow, so the GW volume sent to J1 must equal the drop in aquifer
storage. The test runs copies of this deck with DRY_STEP 0:15, 1:00, 6:00, 24:00.

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
INFILTRATION         HORTON
FLOW_ROUTING         KINWAVE
START_DATE           06/01/2020
START_TIME           00:00:00
REPORT_START_DATE    06/01/2020
REPORT_START_TIME    00:00:00
END_DATE             06/05/2020
END_TIME             00:00:00
WET_STEP             00:05:00
DRY_STEP             24:00:00
REPORT_STEP          01:00:00
ROUTING_STEP         0:00:30

[EVAPORATION]
CONSTANT         0.0

[RAINGAGES]
G1   INTENSITY 1:00 1.0 TIMESERIES R1

[SUBCATCHMENTS]
;;Name Gage Outlet Area %Imperv Width %Slope CurbLen
S1   G1   J1   10.0   0   500   1.0   0

[SUBAREAS]
S1   0.01   0.1   0.05   0.05   0   OUTLET

[INFILTRATION]
S1   3.0   0.5   4   7   0

[AQUIFERS]
;;Name por  WP    FC    Ksat Kslope Tslope ETu  ETs  Seep Ebot Egw Umc
AQ   0.5   0.15   0.30   1.0   10   15   0.35   14   0   0   8   0.30

[GROUNDWATER]
;;Subcatch Aquifer Node Esurf A1 B1 A2 B2 A3 Dsw  (trailing * : see IO-15)
S1   AQ   J1   10   0.05   1.5   0   0   0   0   *

[JUNCTIONS]
J1   2   5   0   0   0

[OUTFALLS]
O1   0   FREE

[CONDUITS]
C1   J1   O1   400   0.013   0   0   0   0

[XSECTIONS]
C1   CIRCULAR   2   0   0   0   1

[TIMESERIES]
R1   06/01/2020 00:00   0.0

[REPORT]
SUBCATCHMENTS ALL
